<title>THAILAND: Thai sugar vessel movements on May 1.</title>
<headline>Thai sugar vessel movements on May 1.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Independent surveyors detailed Thai sugar freight movement as follows (in tonne tel quels):</p>
<p>Vessel		  Position	  Quantity    Destination</p>
<p>Great Concert	SLD Apr 24	 11,000	Indonesia</p>
<p>Pipob Samut	  SLD Apr 27	 15,000	Japan</p>
<p>Dae Gak Bong	 SLD Apr 23	  8,000	Malaysia</p>
<p>Socolf Lake	  SLD Apr 26	  6,000	Singapore</p>
<p>Pitak Samut	  SLD Apr 24	 13,000	Japan</p>
<p>B.U.T. II	    SLD Apr 27	  3,000	China</p>
<p>Hatinh 06	    SLD Apr 28	  1,200	China</p>
<p>Bismihitala	  ETD Apr 28	  9,600	Mombasa</p>
<p>Jilin		  ETD May 05	 11,000	Indonesia</p>
<p>Alam Teladan	 N/A		  16,800	Malaysia</p>
<p>Tropical Rose	N/A		   1,500	Cambodia</p>
<p>Hanbonn Brother    ETD May 03	 13,500	Indonesia</p>
<p>Saint John	   ETD May 04	 14,000	S.Korea</p>
<p>Ban Ann		ETD Apr 30	 14,100	S.Korea</p>
<p>Topaz		  ETD May 02	 13,350	S.Korea</p>
<p>Chile		  ETD May 01	  3,350	Maputo</p>
<p>Alam Tenaga	  ETA May 03	 15,000	Malaysia</p>
<p>Sin Hung 2	   N/A		  12,500	Bangladesh</p>
<p>Alam Teladan	 N/A		  16,800	Malaysia</p>
<p>Bangbunnak	   ETR May 02	  5,500	Indonesia</p>
<p>Bangramard	   ETA May 01	  5,500	Indonesia</p>
<p>Jin Cheng Jiang    ETA May 02	 14,000	China</p>
<p>Myoh Yang 3	  N/A		  12,000	China, N.Korea</p>
<p>Naftolos	     ETA May 08	 18,000	Japan</p>
<p>Yick Zao	     ETA May 05	 29,400	S.Korea</p>
<p>Jin Shan Bao	 ETA May 05	 14,000	China</p>
<p>Tolich		 ETCD Apr 29	12,500	Indonesia</p>
<p>Kwan Bo Mung	 ETA May 04	  8,000	China</p>
<p>Marina Cathya	ETA Apr 29-30     9,500	S.Korea</p>
<p>Sea Harvest	  ETA May 02	 12,000	S.Korea</p>
<p>Pu Cheng	     ETA May 08	 14,000	China</p>
<p>Sonamai		ETA May 26-30     1,300	Cambodia</p>
<p>NOTE: SLD indicates that the vessel has left, ETA = Estimated Time of Arrival, ETD = Estimated Time of Departure, ETR = Estimated Time of Readiness, L/CAN indicated period when vessels are expected in for loading or be cancelled.</p>
</text>
